ion, referencing existing discussion, possibly adjusting recommendation. We have our own notes: Candidate A can anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities, regarded as a show-off, not open to new ideas. Candidate B is very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, weak memory for numbers, makes nasty remarks about colleagues. Candidate C we have many facts. Candidate D responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as a know-it-all, has a hot temper.\n\nWe have already discussed C and B. We haven't discussed A and D. We should bring up A or D. Perhaps we can discuss Candidate A's strengths and concerns, compare with C. Or discuss D. Need to keep argument focused. Could challenge C's communication issues, or bring up A's anticipation of dangerous situations as a strong point. But we must not just dump facts; we need to argue.\n\nWe could say: While C is strong, his egocentric and unwillingness to further education may be problematic for long-term adaptability, and his difficulty communicating could affect crew cooperation. Candidate A shows strong technical competence (anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision) and leadership, but concerns about being a show-off and not open to new ideas may affect crew cooperation and adaptability. Candidate D shows strong problem solving, concentration, responsibility, but has hot temper and know-it-all attitude, which could affect crew cooperation and stress resilience.\n\nWe need to decide whether to keep recommendation C or shift. Likely still C is best, but we need to bring up A and D to satisfy coverage. We can say we still support C but note we need more info on A and D. Or we could propose that A's anticipation of dangerous situations is critical for long-distance flights, maybe outweighs C's communication issues. But we lack info on A's reliability, stress handling, etc. So we might keep C.\n\nThus our contribution: agree with C but note concerns, request more info on A and D. Provide some evidence for A and D. Then vote for C.\n\nWe must include METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\". Provide PUBLIC_MESSAGE.\n\nLet's craft: \"I agree with Agent 3's recommendation of Candidate C. The evidence of stress resilience and technical competence strengthens C's case. However, we still lack data on reliability and stress handling for A and D. Candidate A's ability to anticipate dangerous situations and excellent spatial vision are valuable, but his show\u2011off attitude and resistance to new ideas raise concerns about crew cooperation and adaptability. Candidate D shows strong concentration, problem\u2011solving and responsibility, yet his hot temper and know\u2011it\u2011all perception could impair crew cooperation and stress resilience. Given the current evidence, C remains the strongest overall, but we should still gather any missing observations on A and D before final decision.\"\n\nYes."}
